# Line endings are normalised to LF in the index, so a file's committed bytes do not
# depend on which OS committed it.
#
# This matters beyond tidiness: CI regenerates the ARM conformance goldens and fails on
# any git diff. `regen` writes LF. If a case file were ever committed with CRLF from a
# Windows checkout, the Linux runner would regenerate it to LF and the diff check would
# fail on line endings alone - a red build reporting nothing about the corpus.
* text=auto

# The committed binary fixtures: guest executables, their reference ELFs, and the
# permissively-licensed conformance font. Marked explicitly rather than left to the
# text/binary heuristic, because a false "text" call would corrupt them on checkout.
*.velf binary
*.elf  binary
*.bin  binary
*.ttf  binary
*.png  binary
